id: pm-4pzw7i
title: Declare current pm-changelog commands in the SDK grammar census
description: "Latest published pm-changelog2026.10.23 correctly registers changelog audit and changelog milestone create, but the pm-cli-owned destination/positional census still knows only export and generate. The real command-grammar gate reports two missing_destination and two stale_observed_signature findings after the required latest-package install. Keep generator code upstream unchanged and update the host SDK inventory from the observed package contracts."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T10:53:00.389Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T11:30:13.483Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-23T11:30:12.395Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-23T11:30:12.395Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Current package command destinations are declared as package-owned; Milestone creation retains its required name positional; The real latest-package grammar gate passes without changing grammar budgets or excluding commands
goal: Keep every installed first-party command discoverable through the SDK grammar.
objective: Synchronize the host census with the current published pm-changelog command and positional declarations.
value: A valid latest-package install must not make repository grammar validation reject healthy command registrations.
why_now: The required latest pm-changelog install exposed two newly registered commands during this delivery.
parent: pm-1kxs
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: Installed pm-changelog 2026.10.23 and declared package-owned audit and milestone-create destinations with the required milestone name operand in the host SDK census; upstream generator remains unchanged.
expected_result: All latest-package positional declarations match observed registrations without raising grammar budgets.
actual_result: "Linked suite passes 37 tests. Real installed grammar matches 235 declared and observed signatures, with 20 shapes within the existing 21-shape budget and zero findings. Graph and integrity checks pass."
